# The generated corpus is a cache: minutes of fuzzing rebuild it, and committing
# six megabytes across fifteen hundred files would put it in every clone of this
# repository forever for no gain a reader could use.
#
# `seeds/` is committed and is what a run starts from.
#
# A crash artefact is the opposite and is NOT ignored: `artifacts/` is tracked
# precisely so an input that broke something once is checked on every run after.
corpus/
target/
